I'd like to contribute to the database backends in dplyr.  I see that there are several R files that translate R functions into their SQL equivalents, but there's some fancy stuff going on with argument manipulation, and I'm not sure where to start.

Is there a "introduction for contributors" anywhere?  I've read the databases vignette <https://cran.rstudio.com/web/packages/dplyr/vignettes/databases.html> some of the help for the SQL functions, but those are sparse, particularly with regard to implementation details.

Thanks!

